        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>Breath of Death.</em> A black miasma spills from you and everything in it gets older.</p><p>Each creature in a 15-foot emanation takes @Damage[2d6[void]] damage with a basic Fortitude save. Creatures that fail are <strong>enfeebled 1</strong> for 1 minute as they age; on a critical failure, <strong>enfeebled 2</strong> and <strong>clumsy 1</strong> instead.</p><p>The miasma lingers: until the start of your next turn, an enemy that enters or ends its turn in the area takes <strong>1d6 void</strong> damage with no save.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6, and the lingering damage by 1d6 at every other increment.</p><p><strong>Refined (9th)</strong> The emanation increases to <strong>20 feet</strong>, objects and unattended structures in the area are <strong>broken</strong> (already-broken objects are destroyed), and a creature that critically fails also can't regain Hit Points until the end of its next turn.</p>"
        },
